 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the penal law, in relation to the crime of criminal street gang recruitment of a minor",
    "basePrintNo": "S4898",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4898-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §460.10, add §460.65, Pen L",
    "lawSection": "Penal Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4898\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the penal law, in relation to the crime of criminal\nstreet gang recruitment of a minor\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nCreates the crime of criminal street gang recruitment of a minor.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Amends Section 460.10 of the Penal Law by adding a new\nsubdivision 5. Definitions: \"Criminal street gang\" means any ongoing\norganization, association, or group of three or more persons, whether\nformal or informal, having as one of its primary activities the\ncommission of one or more criminal acts, which has an identifiable\nname or identifying sign or symbol, and whose members individually or\ncollectively engage in or have engaged in criminal street activity.\n\nSection 2. Amends the Penal Law by adding a new section 460.65.\nCriminal street gang recruitment of a minor. A person is guilty of\ncriminal street gang recruitment of a minor when he or she coerces,\nsolicits, recruits or induces a person under sixteen years of age to\njoin or remain a member of a criminal street gang, or conspires to do\nso. Criminal street gang recruitment of a minor is a Class C felony.\n\n3. Effective Date\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nPenal Law; Section 460.10; Definitions; \"criminal street gang\" is not\nin the current list of definitions. Penal Law; Section 460.65;\nCriminal street gang recruitment of a minor and the establishment of a\nClass C felony is a new crime.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nGangs clearly pose a significant threat to community safety. From\nJanuary to mid-October 2009, there were approximately 200\ngang-motivated incidents in New York City. These incidents not only\neffect gang members but often involve innocent victims that are in the\nwrong place at the wrong time. In order to combat the influence that\ngangs have on our youth, it is time that we punish those that actively\nrecruit new members. This legislation would target recruiters of\nstreet gangs by creating the crime of gang recruitment of a minor. A\nperson that is found guilty of criminal street gang recruitment when\nhe or she coerces, recruits or induces a person under sixteen years of\nage to join their gang will be charged with a class C felony.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2016: S.477- REFERRED TO CODES\n2015: S.477- REFERRED TO CODES\n2014: S.14 - Codes 2013: S.14 - Codes\n2012: S.505 - Referred to Children and Families\n2011: S.505 - Discharged from Codes, Committed to Children and\nFamilies\n2009-10: S.6983 - Advanced to Third Reading/A.9971 Referred to Codes\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the first of November next succeeding\nthe date on which it shall have become law.\n",
